comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T06:19:06.152Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live all-status PM inventory has 2732 items with complete source receipts and no omissions; keyword searches for issue numbers and policy authoring/completeness/ownership concepts found no dedicated issue. Existing delivered feature and recovery lineage retained. GitHub has no open PRs or Dependabot/code-scanning alerts; three open reports already have canonical PM link comments."
  "2026-09-11T06:25:40.361Z","harness:codex","TDD and integration evidence: the initial new completeness and policy-id regressions both failed before implementation. All 53 focused tests now pass, including real CLI and MCP policy-id normalization, an assurance floor that fails with no policy, passes with an applicable policy and fails after deletion, and installed governance-audit append flags preserving assignment while edits/deletes refuse. Complete-population duplicate check and the delivered historical foundations are recorded. Full repository coverage, static gates, temporary manual acceptance and hosted review remain required."
  "2026-09-11T06:30:52.462Z","harness:codex","Design decision: compose the existing assurance validate source with a floor on applicable_requirement_count instead of adding a one-off CLI-only strictness flag. The real integration test proves fail/pass/fail across policy creation and deletion, and documentation states that applicability and compliance require independent assertions. Optional state_requirement_count and ungoverned_items bounds support future-state and all-item domain contracts."
  "2026-09-11T06:51:40.284Z","harness:codex","Repository validation evidence: all 2735 current history streams are checked without drift; resolution diagnostics retain the same 170 historical unknowns explicitly documented in the closed pm-e9zh recovery outcome. No placeholder backfill or duplicate cleanup item is appropriate. Complete graph audit has 13636 edges, zero missing targets, zero isolated nodes, zero outcome-unreachable items and an acyclic ordering graph; seven legacy hierarchy exceptions remain advisory. This tranche retains parent, discovered_from and verifies lineage and does not fabricate deep edges."
  "2026-09-11T06:52:11.136Z","harness:codex","Correction to preceding validation summary: the full scan overlapped active linked-test and gate-evidence mutations, so its captured receipt contains three document-hash mismatches on this tranches three actively changing items, not zero drift. All three have now independently passed history --verify --strict-exit with matching current hashes. No chain mismatch or missing stream was observed. A frozen full corpus scan is required after final PM writes; the earlier statement must not be treated as that proof."
  "2026-09-11T06:58:55.634Z","harness:codex","Local implementation verification complete: 8706 tests across 667 files passed; exact coverage 64172/64172 statements, 48869/48869 branches, 13337/13337 functions and 61480/61480 lines. Static quality, typecheck, generated contracts, SDK snapshot, package boundary, docs and exact 100 percent source/export/member docstrings passed. Manual temporary acceptance and linked tests passed. Hosted PR review, analyzer checks and merge remain delivery gates; this closure records implemented behavior, not publication."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T06:45:38.009Z","harness:codex",A clean validation result can be vacuous. Keep applicability counts independent of violation counts and compose numeric assurance assertions rather than introducing transport-specific strict flags.
